<title>JAPAN: Cosmo Oil, Idemitsu say Iraqi oil to arrive May 10.</title>
<headline>Cosmo Oil, Idemitsu say Iraqi oil to arrive May 10.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiners Cosmo Oil Co Ltd and Idemitsu Kosan Co Ltd said on Thursday that the Iraqi crude they bought under a United Nations oil-for-food deal was scheduled to reach Japan around May 10.</p>
<p>Cosmo Oil and Idemitsu both signed contracts to buy 900,000 barrels each of Iraq's Basrah Light crude, and will use the same very large crude carrier (VLCC) to ship it to Chiba, near Tokyo, a Cosmo Oil spokesman said.</p>
<p>Both companies have refineries in Chiba.</p>
<p>Under the U.N. oil-for-food plan, implemented in December, Iraq is allowed to sell $2 billion worth of oil over a period of six months, to buy food and medicine for civilians suffering under sanctions imposed after Iraq invaded Kuwait in 1990.</p>
</text>
